# Enterprise Borrower Domain (CO-DOM-001 / CO-DOM-001A) — Platform Constitution

Status: **ENTERPRISE APPROVED** · Frozen · Canonical borrower identity  
Sprint foundation: **CO-DOM-001** · Domain migration: **CO-DOM-001A**

## Constitutional model

Primary Borrower is **never** assumed to be a Contact.

| `primaryBorrowerKind` | Borrower entity | Contacts role |
|---|---|---|
| `individual` | Contact (`primaryContactId`) | The borrower is the Contact |
| `company` | Company (`companyId`) | Representatives / communication only |

## SSOT

| Concern | Path |
|---|---|
| Kind constants | `src/constants/opportunity-primary-borrower.ts` |
| Identity projection | `src/lib/enterprise-borrower-identity/` |
| Opportunity create (company) | `src/lib/enterprise-opportunity/start-opportunity-from-company.ts` |
| Opportunity create (contact) | `src/lib/enterprise-opportunity/start-opportunity-from-contact.ts` |

## Mandatory consumer rule

Display names, party ids, session context, registry rows, Deal create, runtime projections, Action Center participants, and Move-to-Deal seeds **must** call:

- `resolveOpportunityBorrowerIdentity` / `resolveDealBorrowerIdentity`
- or `borrowerDisplayNameOrDash`

Never:

- `customerName = opportunity.primaryContactName` alone
- `customerId = primaryContactId` alone when `primaryBorrowerKind === company`
- Require `primaryContactId` for Company borrowers

## Forbidden

- Parallel borrower / customer registries
- Treating Company representatives as automatic applicants / guarantors
- Inventing Individual names for Company Opportunities (CAD-2026-001)

